{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_ab3910eb-4c43-4fcc-a3bb-c94132b6ea2a","role":"user","created":1775347341,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_f5b3658ea0804b1390ca00f5","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"subscriptions of MONTHLY TREASURY STATEMENT, MTSRO, for $27.00 per year. \nTo fax your orders (202) 512-2233\n\nThe total cost of my order is $________. International customers please add 25%. Prices include regular domestic postage and handling and are subject to change.\n\nCharge your order. It's Easy!\n\nTo fax your orders (202) 512-2233\n\n| 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| (Company or Personal Name) | (Please type or print) | Please Choose Method of Payment: | Please Choose Method of Payment: |\n| (Additional address/attention line) | nan | Check Payable to the Superintendent of Documents | nan |\n| (Street address) | nan | GPO Deposit Account - | nan |\n| (City, State, ZIP Code) | nan | VISA or MasterCard Account | (Credit card expiration date) |\n| (Daytime phone including area code) | nan | Thank you for your order! | Thank you for your order! |\n| (Purchase Order No.) | YES NO | (Authorizing Signature) | 1291 |\n| May we make your name/address available to other mailers? | nan | Mail To: New Orders, Superintendent of Documents | nan |\n| nan | nan | P.O. Box 371954, Pittsburgh, PA 15250-7954 | nan |\n\nForm can be photocopied\n\nDEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY\nFINANCIAL MANAGEMENT SERVICE\nOFFICE OF THE COMMISSIONER\nWASHINGTON, D.C. 20227\n\nOFFICIAL BUSINESS PENALTY FOR PRIVATE USE, $300\n\nFIRST-CLASS MAIL\nPOSTAGE & FEES PAID\nDepartment of the Treasury\nPermit No. G-4\n\nNew this issue!\n\nPROFILE OF THE ECONOMY Civilian Unemployment Rates\n\nThe unemployment rate edged down to 7.4 percent in October from 7.5 percent the previous month. The rate has now dropped for 4 straight months. That drop reflects fewer people looking for work, rather than higher employment. Earlier in the year, the rate climbed sharply due to a surge in the number of job-seekers, apparently\n\nbased on the view that job prospects had improved. The number of persons counted as unemployed was 9.3 million in October, down about 650,000 from the recent high reached in June. By race, the jobless rate was 6.5 percent for whites, 13.9 percent for blacks (including 42.5 percent for black teenagers), and 11.8 percent for Hispanics.\n\n(Percent)\n\nTREASURY DEPARTMENT LIBRARY\n\nU.S. TREASURY LIBRARY\n\n1 0023328\n\n\n[Output exceeded 2000 line limit (6351 lines total). Full output saved to /tmp/.tmpExHLpG/output-1. Read it with shell commands like `head`, `tail`, or `sed -n '100,200p'` up to 2000 lines at a time.]","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"subscriptions of MONTHLY TREASURY STATEMENT, MTSRO, for $27.00 per year. \nTo fax your orders (202) 512-2233\n\nThe total cost of my order is $________. International customers please add 25%. Prices include regular domestic postage and handling and are subject to change.\n\nCharge your order. It's Easy!\n\nTo fax your orders (202) 512-2233\n\n| 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| (Company or Personal Name) | (Please type or print) | Please Choose Method of Payment: | Please Choose Method of Payment: |\n| (Additional address/attention line) | nan | Check Payable to the Superintendent of Documents | nan |\n| (Street address) | nan | GPO Deposit Account - | nan |\n| (City, State, ZIP Code) | nan | VISA or MasterCard Account | (Credit card expiration date) |\n| (Daytime phone including area code) | nan | Thank you for your order! | Thank you for your order! |\n| (Purchase Order No.) | YES NO | (Authorizing Signature) | 1291 |\n| May we make your name/address available to other mailers? | nan | Mail To: New Orders, Superintendent of Documents | nan |\n| nan | nan | P.O. Box 371954, Pittsburgh, PA 15250-7954 | nan |\n\nForm can be photocopied\n\nDEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY\nFINANCIAL MANAGEMENT SERVICE\nOFFICE OF THE COMMISSIONER\nWASHINGTON, D.C. 20227\n\nOFFICIAL BUSINESS PENALTY FOR PRIVATE USE, $300\n\nFIRST-CLASS MAIL\nPOSTAGE & FEES PAID\nDepartment of the Treasury\nPermit No. G-4\n\nNew this issue!\n\nPROFILE OF THE ECONOMY Civilian Unemployment Rates\n\nThe unemployment rate edged down to 7.4 percent in October from 7.5 percent the previous month. The rate has now dropped for 4 straight months. That drop reflects fewer people looking for work, rather than higher employment. Earlier in the year, the rate climbed sharply due to a surge in the number of job-seekers, apparently\n\nbased on the view that job prospects had improved. The number of persons counted as unemployed was 9.3 million in October, down about 650,000 from the recent high reached in June. By race, the jobless rate was 6.5 percent for whites, 13.9 percent for blacks (including 42.5 percent for black teenagers), and 11.8 percent for Hispanics.\n\n(Percent)\n\nTREASURY DEPARTMENT LIBRARY\n\nU.S. TREASURY LIBRARY\n\n1 0023328\n\n\n[Output exceeded 2000 line limit (6351 lines total). Full output saved to /tmp/.tmpExHLpG/stdout-1. Read it with shell commands like `head`, `tail`, or `sed -n '100,200p'` up to 2000 lines at a time.]","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
