{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347348-ueXVrW457jMxPXlcCFgs","role":"assistant","created":1775347353,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the IFS-1 table with U.S. Reserve Assets data. Looking at the table, I can see the \"Total reserve assets\" column. For the years 1983-1986, I have:\n- 1983: 33747\n- 1984: 34934\n- 1985: 43186\n- 1986r: 48511\n\nI need data for CY1983-1990 inclusive, which includes 1983, 1984, 1985, 1986, 1987, 1988, 1989, 1990. The 1987 data should be in the 1992 bulletin, let me check.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_45f64097c010406e8700b6bc","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"IFS-1\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1992_12.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_f384e402-9f8e-4eba-ad96-ab4d9286ada5","role":"user","created":1775347353,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_45f64097c010406e8700b6bc","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"133:| IFS-1--U.S. Reserve assets | 72.0 |\n2919:Table IFS-1 shows reserve assets of the United States, including gold stock and special drawing rights held in the Special Drawing account in the International Monetary Fund (IMF). The table also shows U.S. reserve holdings and holdings of convertible foreign currencies in the IMF.\n2931:TABLE IFS-1.--U.S. Reserve Assets\n6205:Special drawing rights (\"Exchange Stabilization Fund,\" IFS-1)—International assets created by IMF that serve to increase international liquidity and provide additional international reserves. SDRs may be purchased and sold among eligible holders through IMF. (See IMF.)","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"133:| IFS-1--U.S. Reserve assets | 72.0 |\n2919:Table IFS-1 shows reserve assets of the United States, including gold stock and special drawing rights held in the Special Drawing account in the International Monetary Fund (IMF). The table also shows U.S. reserve holdings and holdings of convertible foreign currencies in the IMF.\n2931:TABLE IFS-1.--U.S. Reserve Assets\n6205:Special drawing rights (\"Exchange Stabilization Fund,\" IFS-1)—International assets created by IMF that serve to increase international liquidity and provide additional international reserves. SDRs may be purchased and sold among eligible holders through IMF. (See IMF.)","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
